  1064 				;
  1065 				; Repurposes BLT_MENU_SEP_CLEAR (bcbs.asm) rather than adding a 13th BCB -
  1066 				; it was the separator's boot-time constant fill, but the separator is now a
  1067 				; 160-byte table loaded straight into VRAM (Load_Menu_Sep, init_vbxe.asm), so
  1068 				; this is its only user.  The 12 BCBs already in bcbs.asm exactly fill the
  1069 				; $100-$1FF VBXE VRAM budget (see the memory-map comment at the top of this
  1070 				; file); a 13th BCB overflowed BLT_NFO_NAME_CLEAR across the $200 boundary
  1071 				; into the NTSC_Palette load and corrupted it - do not add a new BCB here.
  1072 				; Its fixed Dest_Step_X (1) and And mask (0, constant source) already match;
  1073 				; Dest_Step_Y0/1 and Width-1/Height-1 are patched once, up front, since they
  1074 				; don't vary between the 3 kicks (only Dest_Adr/Xor do).
